{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}
    Accueil | {{ parent() }}
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <h1>Welcome to your restaurant inventory management application!</h1>

    <article>
        <p>
            A restaurant inventory management application is like a digital pantry and ledger combined, specifically
            designed to streamline the process of tracking, ordering, and managing stock levels for ingredients,
            supplies, and equipment in a restaurant setting. Here's a breakdown of its functionalities:
        </p>

        <dl>
            <dt>1. Inventory Tracking:</dt>
            <dd>The core feature of the application is to keep a real-time record of all items in stock. It allows
                restaurant staff to easily monitor quantities, expiry dates, and usage patterns of ingredients and
                supplies.
            </dd>
            <dt>2. Ordering and Purchasing:</dt>
            <dd>The application facilitates the ordering process by generating automatic purchase orders when stock
                levels drop below a certain threshold. It can also integrate with suppliers' systems to streamline the
                purchasing workflow.
            </dd>
            <dt>3. Recipe Management:</dt>
            <dd>It enables chefs and kitchen staff to create and store recipes within the application, specifying the
                ingredients required for each dish. This feature helps in accurately tracking ingredient usage and
                calculating the cost of each recipe.
            </dd>
            <dt>4. Forecasting and Analytics:</dt>
            <dd>By analyzing historical data and trends, the application can provide insights into inventory usage
                patterns, helping restaurant owners and managers make informed decisions about stock levels, menu
                planning, and pricing strategies.
            </dd>
            <dt>5. Vendor Management:</dt>
            <dd>It centralizes information about suppliers, including contact details, pricing agreements, delivery
                schedules, and order history, making it easier to manage relationships and negotiate favorable terms.
            </dd>
            <dt>6. Mobile Accessibility:</dt>
            <dd>Many inventory management applications offer mobile compatibility, allowing staff to access inventory
                data, place orders, and update stock levels from anywhere, enhancing flexibility and efficiency.
            </dd>
            <dt>7. Integration with POS Systems:</dt>
            <dd>Integration with the restaurant's Point of Sale (POS) system ensures seamless communication between
                inventory management and sales data, providing a comprehensive view of the business's financial health.
            </dd>
            <dt>8. Alerts and Notifications:</dt>
            <dd>The application can send alerts and notifications to users when stock levels are low, when items are
                about to expire, or when new orders have been placed or received, ensuring timely action and minimizing
                wastage.
            </dd>
        </dl>

        <p>
            Overall, a restaurant inventory management application serves as a vital tool for optimizing operations,
            reducing costs, and ensuring that the kitchen is well-stocked with the necessary ingredients to meet
            customer demand while minimizing waste.
        </p>
    </article>
{% endblock %}
